1. I added a new `location` block `/posts` to catch URLs in the format `/posts/<post_id>`.
2. Inside this block, I used a `rewrite` directive to pass the request to the `api/posts/<post_id>` endpoint.
3. I added a `return` directive to redirect the request to `https://www.askfundu.com/posts/<post_id>`.

Now, when a user visits a post page, they'll see a link in the format `/posts/<post_id>`. When they click on this link, it will redirect them to the same page, but with the `<post_id>` parameter passed to the API endpoint.

